/* The complete export list of every Rations Pedals bundle.
 *
 * --exclude-libs,ALL keeps static archives out of the dynamic symbol table and
 * -fvisibility=hidden keeps our own code out, but neither reaches implicitly
 * instantiated libstdc++ templates: libstdc++ declares `namespace std` with
 * _GLIBCXX_VISIBILITY(default), so an instantiation such as
 * std::vector<double>::_M_fill_assign is emitted WEAK with DEFAULT visibility
 * whatever -fvisibility says, and lands in the bundle's dynamic symbol table.
 *
 * Weak is not unique, so this is not the STB_GNU_UNIQUE bug and glibc will still
 * unload the library. It is still wrong here: with five sibling plug-ins in one
 * host process, the first bundle loaded wins the definition for all five, so
 * five plug-ins that are meant to share nothing at run time would in fact be
 * calling into one another's code. A version script is the only thing that
 * closes it, because it filters the symbol table after everything else has had
 * its say.
 *
 * A VST3 module needs exactly these three entry points and nothing else. */
{
    global:
        GetPluginFactory;
        ModuleEntry;
        ModuleExit;
    local:
        *;
};
